      "message": "active looping doesn\u0027t seem the best idea?\nI\u0027d use an Handler and you\u0027d need to send messages to it to be offloaded to a background thread\nafaik the handler works like a FIFO so it\u0027d have the same properties of the queue\n\n\n```\nmHandlerThread \u003d new HandlerThread(\"ferrochrome input handler\");\nmHandlerThread.start();\n\nmBackgroundHandler \u003d new Handler(mHandlerThread.getLooper()) {\n    @Override\n    public void handleMessage(Message msg) {\n        switch (msg.what) {\n            case EVENT_TOUCH: { sendMultiTouchEventInternal(msg.obj) }\n            case EVENT_TOUCHPAD: {...}\n        }\n}\n\n```\n\nand for example in sendMouseEvent\n```\nMessage.obtain(mBackgroundHandler, EVENT_TOUCH, event).sendToTarget();\n```\n\nfeel free to move forward with this, just wanted to point out an alternative :)",
